# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Bundled third-party binaries (Tesseract/qpdf/pdfium/WebView2/embeddable Python).
# These are laid down by the MSI build on Windows, never committed to this PUBLIC repo
# (size + redistribution hygiene). See docs/packaging.md.
vendor/

# Build artifacts (NOT the build/ source scripts, which ARE committed).
# Only the staging/output dirs the Windows build script writes into:
#   build/stage/  assembled payload tree (embeddable python + site-packages + app)
#   build/out/    produced .msi + wix intermediates
#   build/_dl/    downloaded+verified tool archives (embeddable python, get-pip, ...)
build/stage/
build/out/
build/_dl/
dist/
*.msi
*.wixobj
*.wixpdb

# Rust trusted-core workspace build dirs (incl. the wasm32-wasip2 guest target).
# Cargo.lock IS committed (these crates are apps/bins, not libs). See core/README.md.
core/target/
target/
*.wasm

# Claude Code agent worktrees (transient parallel-agent checkouts under .claude/).
# Never committed — they are isolated working copies of this same repo.
.claude/

# Local app data / matter DBs (should never be in git anyway)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Platform-architecture / strategy DRAFTS staged for review. CLAUDE.md: these are
# kept out of this PUBLIC repo on purpose (the core-module architecture spec is the
# private source of truth). Never commit anything under here.

# Local index created by ./run.sh --demo (fictional sample room only).
.demo-data/

# Chainlink CRE install and local-chain artifacts. The workflow source is committed.
# No .env, no WASM binary, no Foundry cache.
cre/workflow/node_modules/
cre/workflow/.cre_build_tmp.js
cre/contracts/out/
cre/contracts/cache/
cre/contracts/broadcast/
cre/contracts/lib/
cre/.local-sim/
cre/**/.env
.env
